# Copy to .env. Nothing in this repo loads a .env on its own — the drivers are
# run with `node --env-file=.env`, and exporting these in your shell works
# just as well. Every variable here is optional except the key, and the key is
# only needed for the paths that spend money: the app's deploy button and the
# matrix driver. Browsing the seeded app, rebuilding the tables, and checking
# the published numbers all work with this file absent.

# Read by the Anthropic SDK itself (`new Anthropic()` in lib/anthropic/call.ts
# takes no explicit key). Required for any real call.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The spend gate's ceiling, in dollars, checked per call from outside the loop.
# Unset means the gate has nothing to refuse against — that is the shipped
# default, so a measurement run can reach its natural end. Name a number here
# before any run you would not want to be able to overrun. It is a worst-case
# projection, not a hard bound; see "Run the agent itself" in the README.
# DELEGATE_CEILING_USD=0.40

# Port for the live meter (scripts/usage-dashboard.mjs). The app itself is
# fixed at 3939 by the `dev` and `start` scripts in package.json.
# PORT=8080
